+### Pick New Host
+
+In a floor or ceiling plan, select one door or window and choose **Pick New Host** from its contextual Modify tools or
+right-click menu. Point at another wall to preview the placement, then click. **Esc** cancels. One **Undo** restores the
+old host and position. A project edit or a view change cancels a pending placement.
+
+The opening keeps its identity, mark, type/family, instance values and sill. Its hand and facing remain relative to the
+new wall's interior/exterior faces, so reversing the target wall can reverse its orientation in world coordinates.
+A family's geometry follows the new wall thickness. The old wall's hole closes and the new wall is cut.
+For a family with a moved origin, offset and sill still locate that insertion point. Rehosting preserves the family's
+origin and the opening's physical height; a valid stored sill can be negative when its physical bottom is above the base.
+
+This first version supports ordinary straight walls on the **same level and base elevation**. Unpin the opening first.
+Curved/slanted/profiled/curtain walls, curtain panel replacement walls, grouped openings/walls and Edit Group are unsupported. The action
+is disabled outside plans. This is an explicit command, not dragging between walls. Invalid placement leaves the model
+unchanged; existing width, overlap and sill-fit rules apply.
